{% comment %}
  Appx — Product Specs Table
  Resolves ONE data row's value cell against the live product (slice 2,
  `context/features/35-storefront-value-part-resolution.md`).

  Params (render scope is isolated — both must be passed explicitly):
  - row:     one DATA row object from the metaobject `rows` json field
  - product: the current product (drives SHOPIFY_FIELD / METAFIELD parts)

  Contracts:
  - Emits the resolved cell HTML only — no wrapper element. The block captures
    this output and applies the whole-cell `hideWhenEmpty` gate; keep all
    author-meaningful whitespace (TEXT part edges like "Up to ") intact.
  - Every dynamic value is escaped before output (merchant/Shopify data is
    never trusted as HTML). The only raw HTML emitted is `<br>` (LINE_BREAK
    and metafield multiline newlines via `newline_to_br` AFTER `escape`).
  - Variant-sourced fields read `product.first_available_variant`, falling
    back to the FIRST variant when every variant is unavailable (sold-out
    products must still show their specs). Selected-variant resolution +
    live variant-switch JS are deferred (locked decision).
  - Shopify caps `{% for %}` at 50 iterations, so the parts loop runs in
    50-part chunks (a long multiline value alone can exceed 50 parts).
  - Unknown/unresolvable tokens emit nothing (silent by design), including
    `total_inventory` (no clean product-level Liquid property).
  - METAFIELD parts resolve down THREE paths, because `metafield_text` alone
    covers only some of the type space (see the branches below):
      1. metaobject-backed (`metaobject_reference`, `list.metaobject_reference`
         — what ALL of Shopify's standard `shopify.*` taxonomy choice-list
         attributes are) → the filter WITH its `field:` parameter.
      2. any OTHER list type → rendered here, item by item; the filter emits
         nothing at all for them.
      3. everything else → the filter, unparameterised.
  - `selected_options` renders `variant.title` (the option values joined with
    " / ", guaranteed string) and emits nothing for single-variant products —
    shoppers must never see "Default Title".
  - `inventory_quantity` guard: untracked inventory (`inventory_management`
    nil) returns "items sold", which would mislead shoppers — emit nothing.
  - `weight` guard: 0 means unset — emit nothing rather than "0 g".
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign variant = product.first_available_variant | default: product.variants.first
  assign part_chunks = row.valueParts.size | plus: 49 | divided_by: 50
-%}
{%- for chunk in (1..part_chunks) -%}
  {%- assign part_offset = chunk | minus: 1 | times: 50 -%}
  {%- for part in row.valueParts offset: part_offset limit: 50 -%}
    {%- case part.type -%}
      {%- when "TEXT" -%}{{ part.text | escape }}
      {%- when "LINE_BREAK" -%}<br>
      {%- when "METAFIELD" -%}
        {%- assign mf = product.metafields[part.namespace][part.key] -%}
        {%- assign mf_type = mf.type | default: "" -%}
        {%- if mf_type contains "metaobject_reference" -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            `metafield_text` renders NOTHING for `metaobject_reference` /
            `list.metaobject_reference` unless it is given the `field:` parameter
            naming which field of the referenced metaobject to print — the filter
            has no default field. That is not an edge case: every choice-list
            attribute in Shopify's standard product taxonomy (the whole `shopify`
            namespace — `shopify.battery-type`, `shopify.power-source`,
            `shopify.color-pattern`, …) is metaobject-backed, and the metafield
            picker offers those definitions like any other. So the un-parameterised
            call silently emitted an empty cell for them.

            Shopify's taxonomy metaobjects name their display field `label`; custom
            merchant definitions commonly use `name` or `title`. Try them in that
            order and take the first non-blank — `field:` may only reference a
            `single_line_text_field`, and a miss renders blank rather than raising.
            All three blank stays SILENT, consistent with the unknown-token rule.

            Going through the filter (rather than walking `mf.value` by hand) keeps
            the single/list split inside Shopify's implementation: a list renders in
            sentence format ("A, B, and C") and is not subject to the 50-iteration
            `for` cap.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign mo_text = mf | metafield_text: field: "label" -%}
          {%- if mo_text == blank -%}{%- assign mo_text = mf | metafield_text: field: "name" -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if mo_text == blank -%}{%- assign mo_text = mf | metafield_text: field: "title" -%}{%- endif -%}
          {{- mo_text | escape -}}
        {%- elsif mf_type contains "list." and mf_type != "list.single_line_text_field" -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            `metafield_text` supports NO list type except `list.single_line_text_field`
            and `list.metaobject_reference` — both handled elsewhere — so every other
            list (`list.number_integer`, `list.dimension`, `list.product_reference`,
            `list.color`, …) rendered an empty cell. Those are rendered here instead,
            one item at a time.

            🔴 The per-item shape is DUCK-TYPED, not switched on `mf_type`, and that is
            deliberate. Shopify's measurement family is open and still growing — the
            type list already carries `dimension`, `weight`, `volume`, `voltage`,
            `temperature`, `speed`, `antenna_gain`, `volumetric_flow_rate` and more —
            but every one of them is the same `measurement` object (`.value` + `.unit`).
            A `case mf_type` would silently drop each new member the day Shopify ships
            it; testing for `.unit` cannot. Same reasoning for the reference types:
            they differ only in which display property they carry.

            Order matters — the chain runs most specific first. A plain string / number
            / date answers `nil` to every property test and falls through to `{{ item }}`,
            which is exactly right for the scalar lists.

            SIZE: reference lists are CONNECTIONS and answer `.count`; non-reference
            lists are arrays and answer `.size` (metafield object docs, "Determining the
            length of a list metafield"). Lists run to 128 items (256 for metaobject
            references) against a 50-iteration `for` cap, so this chunks exactly like
            the parts loop above.

            ⚠️ DIVERGENCE, accepted: Shopify renders its two supported list types in
            localized sentence format ("A, B, and C"); this joins with ", ". Matching it
            would mean hardcoding an English "and" (an i18n bug on a translated
            storefront) or adding a locale key plus last-item lookahead that the
            blank-skip below makes unreliable. A comma list also reads better in a spec
            table. The two Shopify-rendered types keep their sentence format — this is
            not worth regressing a live-verified path over.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign list_items = mf.value -%}
          {%- assign list_size = list_items.count | default: list_items.size | default: 0 -%}
          {%- assign list_chunks = list_size | plus: 49 | divided_by: 50 -%}
          {%- assign printed = 0 -%}
          {%- for list_chunk in (1..list_chunks) -%}
            {%- assign list_offset = list_chunk | minus: 1 | times: 50 -%}
            {%- for item in list_items offset: list_offset limit: 50 -%}
              {%- capture item_text -%}
                {%- if item.unit != blank -%}{{ item.value }} {{ item.unit }}
                {%- elsif item.rating != blank -%}{{ item.rating }}
                {%- elsif item.title != blank -%}{{ item.title }}
                {%- elsif item.name != blank -%}{{ item.name }}
                {%- elsif item.url != blank -%}{{ item.url }}
                {%- elsif item.src != blank -%}{{ item.src }}
                {%- else -%}{{ item }}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endcapture -%}
              {%- assign item_text = item_text | strip -%}
              {%- if item_text != blank -%}
                {%- if printed > 0 -%}, {% endif -%}
                {{- item_text | escape -}}
                {%- assign printed = printed | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- mf | metafield_text | escape | newline_to_br -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- when "SHOPIFY_FIELD" -%}
        {%- case part.field -%}
          {%- when "vendor" -%}{{ product.vendor | escape }}
          {%- when "product_type" -%}{{ product.type | escape }}
          {%- when "category" -%}{{ product.category.name | escape }}
          {%- when "tags" -%}{{ product.tags | join: ", " | escape }}
          {%- when "available_for_sale" -%}{%- if product.available -%}{{ "spec_table.available_yes" | t }}{%- else -%}{{ "spec_table.available_no" | t }}{%- endif -%}
          {%- when "selected_options" -%}{%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}{{ variant.title | escape }}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- when "price" -%}{{ variant.price | money }}
          {%- when "compare_at_price" -%}{%- if variant.compare_at_price -%}{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}{%- endif -%}
          {%- when "sku" -%}{{ variant.sku | escape }}
          {%- when "barcode" -%}{{ variant.barcode | escape }}
          {%- when "weight" -%}{%- if variant.weight > 0 -%}{{ variant.weight_in_unit | weight_with_unit: variant.weight_unit }}{%- endif -%}
          {%- when "inventory_quantity" -%}{%- if variant.inventory_management -%}{{ variant.inventory_quantity }}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endfor -%}
